You define a namespace using the `namespace` keyword, followed by its name and curly braces:
```cpp
namespace Network {
    class Socket { /* ... */ };
    void connect() { /* ... */ }
}
```

You can define nested namespaces directly or sequentially. To access `port` using an alias:
```cpp
namespace App {
    namespace Config {
        int port = 8080;
    }
}

// ...

namespace AC = App::Config; // Define alias
std::cout << AC::port; // Access using alias
```
